makedep reads .cpp sources like .c sources, for Valve's lsteamclient, whose Unix half is C++.

From ValveSoftware/wine, branch proton_11.0 (LGPL-2.1-or-later), by Valve: the same table line in
tools/makedep.c, without the rest of Valve's C++ support. clang compiles .cpp as C++ by its extension,
and a C++ file's '#pragma makedep unix' then puts it in the module's Unix library.

The Wine tree has no .cpp file, so this changes nothing in the engine's own build. It lets Valve's
lsteamclient (its Unix half is C++), built as its own archive, build against this tree with Wine's own
make. Without it makedep compiles a .cpp file as a Windows object.

Upstream status: Valve's Proton patch, carried with patch 0004 as part of the Steam bridge.

--- a/tools/makedep.c
+++ b/tools/makedep.c
@@ -1237,6 +1237,7 @@
 } parse_functions[] =
 {
     { ".c",   parse_c_file },
+    { ".cpp", parse_c_file },
     { ".h",   parse_c_file },
     { ".inl", parse_c_file },
     { ".l",   parse_c_file },
